course: dictionary
lesson: 555
title: Attractive: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «We walked through an attractive garden full of roses.» Here attractive means pleasant to look at, or pretty.
explain: Now read this: «The shop made an attractive offer: two for the price of one.» Nobody is talking about looks here. Attractive means interesting and appealing, so you want to take it. Ask yourself: what is the sentence really about?
explain: Science uses the word too. An attractive force pulls things towards each other. North and south ends of magnets are attractive to each other, so they pull together. Same word, different meaning: the clues tell you which one.
fact: Attractive means pleasant to look at, good-looking or pretty.
fact: Attractive also means interesting or appealing, making you want it.
fact: In science, an attractive force pulls things towards each other, like magnetism or gravity.
fact: «Plain» said about a person's looks means not attractive.
fact: In London slang, «peng» means great or attractive, and «innit» means «isn't it».
exercise: «We walked through an attractive garden full of roses.» What does attractive mean here? | Cold and wet | Dangerous and steep | Very loud | *Pleasant to look at
exercise: «The shop made an attractive offer: two for the price of one.» What does attractive mean here? | Good-looking | *Interesting, making you want it | Very old | Pulling things together
exercise: In science, what does an attractive force do? | Turns things into water | *Pulls things towards each other | Makes things glow | Pushes things far apart
test: Which sentence uses attractive to mean interesting or appealing? | The attractive bridge crossed the river. | The attractive lake was calm and blue. | *The attractive price made everyone queue at the till.
test: Which word means not attractive when said about a person's looks? | *Plain | Gravity | Rubenesque | Peng
exam: In «The magnet had an attractive pull on the paper clip», what does attractive mean? | *It pulls things towards each other, as a science force | Interesting, like an offer | Very old | Pleasant to look at
